A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

## The rule

A report is a duplicate only when the evidence supports the same underlying cause. This
is proposed in [decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) to replace the subject-only
rule in [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject), pending desk approval.

1. Read the report and look for matching symptoms and conditions.
2. Check the tenant locale, form version, channel, and available evidence.
3. Merge only when the same cause is supported; otherwise keep it separate for investigation.

<Callout>
Similar subjects can hide different causes. Record uncertainty instead of merging by default.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Keep the report separate, record what is unknown, and ask the support desk to investigate.
